{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-per-nucleon-channel-decomposition","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:per-nucleon-channel-decomposition","kind":"definition","title":"Per-nucleon channel decomposition via $S_3^A$ branching","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-typed-crossing-operator"],"tags":["branching","channel-decomposition","garside","hecke-algebra","per-nucleon","torus-knot"],"defines":["per-nucleon-channel-decomposition"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.PerNucleonChannelDecomposition","text":"per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.md","leanSource":"per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:per-nucleon-channel-decomposition\"></a><p><em>The <dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-per-nucleon-channel-decomposition\">per-nucleon channel decomposition</dfn> of the typed Garside element for a nucleus of mass number <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> is the factorization</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  G(c_1, \\ldots, c_A)\n  = \\prod_{m=1}^{A} G_{n_m}(c_m),</code></pre>\n<p><em>where each per-nucleon factor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_{n_m}(c_m)</code> is the expectation value of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_3</code> in the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,3}</code> eigenvector of channel <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_m</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n_m \\in \\{P, N\\}</code> is the nucleon type, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_m \\in \\{\\mathrm{triv}, \\mathrm{conf}, \\mathrm{unconf}, \\mathrm{sign}\\}</code> ranges over the four channels of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,3}</code> eigenstructure of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_3(q)</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.md","heading":"Definition","number":"14.10.1","page":"b/def-per-nucleon-channel-decomposition","qa":{"counts":{"pass":80,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Confinement.PerNucleonChannelDecomposition","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/per-nucleon-channel-decomposition.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
